  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rSite Location Plan 1808/00 Dated June 2026\rFloor Plans and Elevations as Existing 1808/01 Dated June 2026\rFloor Plans and Rear Elevation as Proposed 1808/02 Rev B Dated June 2026\rPlanning, Design and Access Statement \rHighway Safety Impact Form\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than five residents at any one time without first obtaining the approval, in writing, of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen and dining/living rooms shall be retained in perpetuity. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Within SIX months from the date of this decision, cycle parking, as indicated on drawing \"Floor Plans and Rear Elevation as Proposed 1808/02 Rev B Dated June 2026\", shall be provided within the site in accordance with the following requirements:\r\ro Provision of a minimum of FIVE long stay cycle parking spaces.\r\ro in an accessible location: the access route to the long stay store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should involve no more than 2 doors or gates (excluding the store door) which must also have a minimum opening width of 1.2m;\r\ro secured: with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob;\r\ro fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of accessible, secure, and adequate cycle parking facilities and to safeguard the character and appearance of the area.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site have been provided within the development, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rNo refuse storage containers or sacks shall be stored on Green Lanes or Park Avenue except on refuse collection days as per the Council's published collection schedule.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the occupiers of adjoining premises; protect the general environment; prevent any obstruction to pedestrian movement and to ensure that there are adequate facilities for the storage and recycling of recoverable materials.\r",
    "Within six months of the date of this permission, the first-floor shared kitchen and adjoining ancillary space shall be arranged and furnished to provide a communal dining area for all five occupiers. The dining area shall include seating for at least five people and either a suitably sized dining table or a wall-mounted counter table, appropriate to the narrow layout of the space. The dining area shall thereafter be retained and kept available for communal use.\r\rReason: To provide suitable communal living facilities and ensure an acceptable standard of accommodation for the occupiers of the HMO.\r"
  ],
